      "content": "Your intuition is correct, the body does try to replenish iron levels on its own. However, the rate of replenishment is not as fast as you think, and giving your daughter a high dose of iron will not magically accelerate her recovery. In fact, taking too much iron at once can cause a phenomenon called iron overload, where the excess iron builds up in the body and can cause more harm than good. I recommend taking the recommended dose and monitoring her progress, but I also suggest you talk to her doctor about adjusting the dose or adding other supplements to help boost her iron levels more quickly.",
